Correct. The probability of getting exactly 6 heads in 10 fair coin flips is

\[
P(X=6)=\binom{10}{6}\left(\frac12\right)^{10}
=\frac{210}{1024}
=\frac{105}{512}
\approx 0.2051
\]

So the probability is

\[
\boxed{\frac{105}{512}\approx 20.51\%}
\]

